{"id":"CVE-2006-4790","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2006-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T19:23:41.157Z","description":"verify.c in GnuTLS before 1.4.4, when using an RSA key with exponent 3, does not properly handle excess data in the digestAlgorithm.parameters field when generating a hash, which allows remote attackers to forge a PKCS #1 v1.5 signature that is signed by that RSA key and prevents GnuTLS from correctly verifying X.509 and other certificates that use PKCS, a variant of CVE-2006-4339.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/25762","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"25762"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/22992","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"22992"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/21937","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"21937"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/22049","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"22049"},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1016844","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1016844"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2006/3899","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2006-3899"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/20027","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"20027"},{"url":"http://www.novell.com/linux/security/advisories/2006_23_sr.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SR:2006:023"},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDKSA-2006:166","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDKSA-2006:166"},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2006-0680.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2006:0680"},{"url":"http://www.gnu.org/software/gnutls/security.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://oval.cisecu