{"id":"CVE-2006-7239","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-05-24T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T20:57:41.045Z","description":"The _gnutls_x509_oid2mac_algorithm function in lib/gnutls_algorithms.c in GnuTLS before 1.4.2 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) via a crafted X.509 certificate that uses a hash algorithm that is not supported by GnuTLS, which triggers a NULL pointer dereference.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.gnu.org/software/gnutls/security.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnutls-dev/2006-August/001192.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-dev] 20060812 GnuTLS 1.4.2"},{"url":"http://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnutls-dev/2006-August/001190.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-dev] 20060812 Re: [Fwd: crash in GNUTLS-1.4.0]"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
